From 3117070b7554dbe7dc2dd89d68f39bbb19bcb101 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kob <kob@invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:09:57 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] Strict reads on any workload

Strict mode was tied to background analysis: a strict SegmentReader always
fetched on Health or Warm, and playback could only fill gaps with zeros or TS
null packets. SegmentReader::strict(bool) and vfs::Reader::strict(bool) now
switch strictness alone, and with_workload picks the workload (Stream by
default). A strict read errors on a gap or a copy no provider serves exactly as
posted, serves bodies only once whole (so a CRC failure is never streamed out),
and asks providers for known holes. Playback keeps prewarm, hedges and the
on-demand refetch of a failed head; health and warming reads keep none.
